+# Collaborative Document Editor — CONTRACT
+
+## 1. REST API
+
+| # | Behavior | Verification |
+|---|----------|-------------|
+| 1.1 | `POST /documents` accepts `{title: string}` and returns `201 {id, title, content, createdAt, updatedAt}` | `curl -X POST -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"title":"Test"}' http://localhost:PORT/documents` |
+| 1.2 | `GET /documents` returns a list (array) of all documents | `curl http://localhost:PORT/documents` → `[{id, title, content, createdAt, updatedAt}]` |
+| 1.3 | `GET /documents/:id` returns a single document by ID | `curl http://localhost:PORT/documents/CREATED_ID` |
+| 1.4 | `GET /documents/:id` returns `404` for unknown IDs | `curl http://localhost:PORT/documents/nonexistent` → 404 |
+| 1.5 | `PUT /documents/:id` updates title and/or content, returns updated doc with updated `updatedAt` | `curl -X PUT -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"title":"New","content":"hi"}' http://localhost:PORT/documents/ID` |
+| 1.6 | `DELETE /documents/:id` deletes a document and returns `204` | `curl -X DELETE http://localhost:PORT/documents/ID` → 204 |
+| 1.7 | `DELETE /documents/:id` returns `404` for unknown IDs | `curl -X DELETE http://localhost:PORT/documents/nonexistent` → 404 |
+| 1.8 | `GET /documents/:id/versions` returns an array of version history entries | `curl http://localhost:PORT/documents/ID/versions` → `[{version, content, operation, createdAt}]` |
+| 1.9 | Creating a doc via POST creates version 1 with empty content | Check `GET /documents/:id/versions` has version 1 |
+| 1.10 | Each PUT update creates a new version entry | Check versions list grows after PUT |
+
+## 2. WebSocket Protocol
+
+| # | Behavior | Verification |
+|---|----------|-------------|
+| 2.1 | Connecting to `ws://host:PORT/ws/:docId` succeeds | WebSocket client connects without error |
+| 2.2 | Server sends `{type: "init", content, version, docId}` upon connection | Client receives one message after connect |
+| 2.3 | Unknown docId on connect causes server to close with error | Client receives close frame with error |
+| 2.4 | Client can send `{type: "op", version: N, op: {type: "insert", pos, text}}` | No error response from server |
+| 2.5 | Client can send `{type: "op", version: N, op: {type: "delete", pos, length}}` | No error response from server |
+| 2.6 | Server broadcasts operations to ALL connected clients (including sender) | Second client connected to same doc receives the op broadcast |
+| 2.7 | Broadcast messages have `{type: "op", version, op}` shape | Inspect broadcast payload |
+| 2.8 | Server rejects invalid JSON with `{type: "error", message}` | Send garbage → receive error |
+| 2.9 | Server rejects ops with negative positions with error | Send `{type:"op", version:1, op:{type:"insert", pos:-1, text:"x"}}` → error |
+| 2.10 | Server rejects ops with positions past end of content with error | Send delete past end of document → error |
+
+## 3. Operational Transform
+
+| # | Behavior | Verification |
+|---|----------|-------------|
+| 3.1 | `apply("hello", {type:"insert", pos:0, text:"X"})` → `"Xhello"` | Unit test |
+| 3.2 | `apply("hello", {type:"delete", pos:1, length:2})` → `"hlo"` | Unit test |
+| 3.3 | `transform(insert(3,"A"), insert(1,"B"))` → `insert(4,"A")` (pos shifted by B's length) | Unit test |
+| 3.4 | `transform(insert(0,"A"), insert(3,"B"))` → `insert(0,"A")` (no shift needed) | Unit test |
+| 3.5 | `transform(insert(0,"A"), delete(1,2))` → `insert(0,"A")` (insert before delete) | Unit test |
+| 3.6 | `transform(insert(5,"A"), delete(1,2))` → `insert(3,"A")` (insert shifted by delete length) | Unit test |
+| 3.7 | `transform(delete(3,2), insert(1,"XXX"))` → `delete(6,2)` (pos shifted by insert) | Unit test |
+| 3.8 | `transform(delete(1,2), delete(3,2))` → `delete(1,2)` (before, no shift) | Unit test |
+| 3.9 | `transform(delete(4,2), delete(1,2))` → `delete(2,2)` (shifted) | Unit test |
+| 3.10 | Concurrent inserts at same position: both preserved (tie-breaking by client id) | Unit test |
+| 3.11 | Insert inside deleted range moves to deletion point | Unit test |
+
+## 4. Persistence
+
+| # | Behavior | Verification |
+|---|----------|-------------|
+| 4.1 | Documents survive server restart (when using persistent DB path) | Create doc, stop server, create new server with same DB, GET returns doc |
+| 4.2 | Version history survives server restart | Create doc, update it, stop, restart, GET versions still shows history |
+| 4.3 | Document content matches the latest version | Compare `GET /documents/:id` content with versions entry |
+
+## 5. Concurrent Collaboration
+
+| # | Behavior | Verification |
+|---|----------|-------------|
+| 5.1 | Two clients connected to same doc both receive init message | Both get init with same content |
+| 5.2 | Edit from client A appears on client B | Send op from A, B receives broadcast with matching content |
+| 5.3 | Concurrent edits from two clients both applied (no lost operations) | A inserts at pos 0, B inserts at pos 5 simultaneously; both insertions appear in final content |
+| 5.4 | Three or more concurrent clients all converge to same state | Each sends 5 random ops; final content is identical on all |
+| 5.5 | 10 concurrent clients producing 100+ total ops converge without corruption | All clients see same final content, content matches REST API |
+
+## 6. Server Lifecycle
+
+| # | Behavior | Verification |
+|---|----------|-------------|
+| 6.1 | `createApp()` returns `{app, start, stop}` | TypeScript interface check |
+| 6.2 | `start()` starts listening and returns the port number | Call start(0) → returns a number > 0 |
+| 6.3 | `stop()` closes all connections and stops the server | After stop, server port is no longer listening |
+| 6.4 | `start()` without port argument uses a random available port | Port returned is > 0 |
+| 6.5 | Multiple `createApp()` instances can coexist on different ports | Create two apps, start on different ports, both work |
+| 6.6 | `stop()` called when server not started is safe (no error) | Call stop() on a fresh createApp() — no throw |
+
+## 7. Input Validation & Robustness
+
+| # | Behavior | Verification |
+|---|----------|-------------|
+| 7.1 | POST /documents without title returns 400 | `{"message":"title is required"}` |
+| 7.2 | PUT /documents/:id with empty body is valid (no-op update) | Returns existing doc unchanged |
+| 7.3 | Malformed WebSocket messages are caught and return error, don't crash | Send binary data, send invalid JSON → error response |
+| 7.4 | Server handles rapid-fire messages without crashing | Send 50 ops in rapid succession on one connection |
+| 7.5 | Client disconnect does not affect other clients | Disconnecting one client, others continue to work |
+
+## 8. Version History
+
+| # | Behavior | Verification |
+|---|----------|-------------|
+| 8.1 | Version entries have incrementing version numbers | `[1, 2, 3, ...]` |
+| 8.2 | Version entries store the full content at that version | Content field matches after applying all ops up to that version |
+| 8.3 | Version entries store the operation that produced them | Operation field is non-null |
